From 36a995112380b3e1e7d64c3821ee7bc023413c98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:56:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/28] Fix the start-up heartbeat replay blackout; publication
 follows the effective ACL (B1); review fixes

WP1 (claude-sonnet-5-5): the transport retains one heartbeat per holder per minute, and the core
consumer replayed the first, empty start-up beat after fresher ones, retracting every holder's
domains and terms for ~3 s; org.holder_heartbeat now ignores snapshots older than the applied one.
Term/entity publication now uses the disclosure-time ACL (source visibility, exportable, disclosure,
access state, selection), drops deny_patterns, and publishes nothing without a server secret; bounded
minimum-unit cover search. ENGINEER-E (claude-sonnet-5-5): REVIEW_E F1-F4. Full suite 507 passed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QgQYqiZ8KjrbuXgxGadraA
